<!--
  Hexapod robot description (6 legs x 3 DOF: coxa-femur-tibia, 18 x TD-8135MG servo)
  Source CAD : final1.SLDASM  -> exported STEP AP214 -> tools/gen.py
  Frames     : REP-103 (x forward, y left, z up). base_link = geometric centre of the body plate.
               base_link is a massless root; body_link (mesh + inertia) is fixed to it with an
               identity transform, so both frames coincide (avoids the KDL "root link has an
               inertia" warning and keeps the body_link name used by hexapod_kinematics).
  Names      : legs front_left, middle_left, rear_left, front_right, middle_right, rear_right;
               joints <leg>_{coxa,femur,tibia}_joint; links <leg>_{coxa,femur,tibia,foot}_link.
               These are the ros2_ws interface (hexapod_kinematics.LEGS, controllers, bridge) -
               do not rename without updating those packages.
  Zero pose  : coxa pointing radially outward along its mounting direction,
               femur horizontal, tibia (knee -> foot-sphere centre) pointing straight down.
  Positive joint direction:
               coxa  : counter-clockwise seen from above (+z of base_link)
               femur : lifts the knee (foot goes up)
               tibia : swings the foot outward/upward
-->
